            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mississippi\u2019s Gestational Age Act prohibits abortions after fifteen (15) weeks of gestation, except in a medical emergency or severe fetal abnormality."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Jackson Women's Health Organization",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70091abee490f2ed61351bd072823e0743d6dd01b6f664359dbcf25bc755e0ad",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70091abee490-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Jackson Women's Health Organization, Jackson Women\u2019s Health Organization challenged the Act, alleging it violates the constitutional right to abortion established in Roe v. Wade and Planned Parenthood v. Casey."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8032270447a8c06eb326e1e640dbd007aa7e193330a0607cf8e44aeac9951e56",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8032270447a8-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, the Court\u2019s certified question was whether all pre\u2011viability prohibitions on elective abortions are unconstitutional."
      }
    ],
